**Declared actions.** This step MUST do exactly these, and the worker base prompt says what each verb obliges:
- `ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.StudyViewTests`

**How to implement.** The study view's first flow step, Unknowns: the kit's studies, a New study form, the study's experiments and opened materials, and the unknowns table (001 §O 'Study view: the unknowns table (owner, scope, fix / free, bounds, priors, links)'; 001 §O 'a left flow strip: Items → Setups → Experiments → Data → Unknowns → Plan → Fit → Results → Publish, each step reachable directly'; 001 §P `CreateStudy`, `AddExperimentsToStudy`, `OpenMaterial`, `SetParameterScope`, `LinkParameters`; the S11.5 brief; .spec-md §3.22: a step appears when it works). The study's steps are the Inverse constructor's alone, as Data is (step 323), because studies fit measured data. The surface is a step of the kit window, not a window, so no `WindowFit.keepOnScreen` call is added; it joins `ScrollExtentTests` (.spec-md §4 'UI'). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.5. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, a group after the Data step's (step 323) under `// --- The study's Unknowns step (StudyUnknownsView). ---`, each member with a one-line doc: `flowUnknownsStep` (`"FlowUnknownsStep"`), `studyUnknownsPanel` (`"StudyUnknownsPanel"`), `studyList` (`"StudyList"`), `studyStatusLine` (`"StudyStatusLine"`), `newStudyNameField` (`"NewStudyNameField"`), `createStudyButton` (`"CreateStudyButton"`), `studyExperimentsText` (`"StudyExperimentsText"`) and `studyUnknownsGrid` (`"StudyUnknownsGrid"`). (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`, each with a one-line doc citing spec 0050 S11.5: `studyChoice (name : StudyName)` is `StudyChoice_<the name's file stem>`; `newStudyExperimentToggle (name : ExperimentName)` is `NewStudyExperiment_<its file stem>`; `addExperimentToStudyButton (name : ExperimentName)` is `AddExperimentToStudy_<its file stem>`; `openMaterialButton (version : MaterialVersionId)` is `OpenMaterial_<the GUID>_v<n>`; and `studyParameterRow`, `studyParameterScopeChoice` and `studyParameterLinkChoice (parameter : StudyParameterRef)` are `StudyParameterRow_`, `StudyParameterScope_` and `StudyParameterLink_` followed by `<the item's GUID>_<name>` or `<the material's GUID>_v<n>_<name>`, one private helper writing that key. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: `ConstructorFlowStep` (steps 238, 242, 323) gains `UnknownsFlowStep` after `DataFlowStep`, its `caption` `Unknowns` and its `flowUiId` `flowUnknownsStep`; `all` lists Items, Setups, Experiments, Data and Unknowns, and `stepsOf ForwardConstructor` answers `all` without Data and the study's steps. `ShowFlowStep` of a step `stepsOf model.constructorMode` lacks changes nothing, and `ShowFlowStep UnknownsFlowStep` otherwise sets `flowStep` alone, the open bay kept; `SwitchConstructorMode ForwardConstructor` from a step `stepsOf ForwardConstructor` lacks lands on `ExperimentsFlowStep` with `BayNames.experiments`, as from Data (step 323). On the model extension holding `studyContext` (step 410): `member model.studyParameterCaption (parameter : StudyParameterRef) : ControlCaption`, `<the item's label> <name>` or `<the material's name> v<n> <name>` (a material named through `model.materials.resolveVersion`, its GUID when that answers nothing), documented in one line. (4) New `OpticalConstructor.Ui/StudyUnknownsView.fs`, `module OpticalConstructor.Ui.StudyUnknownsView`, compiled directly after `DataStepView.fs` (step 323) and before `KitWindowView.fs`: one `<Compile>` line and no comment; its module doc one to three lines citing 001 §O and spec 0050 S11.5. (a) `studyBarView (model : TableAndElementRotationModel) (dispatch : TableAndElementRotationMsg -> unit) : IView`, the head every study surface shows (steps 415, 417, 418): the semi-bold `Study:`, a `WrapPanel` carrying `studyList` with one box per study of `kitStudies` carrying `studyChoice` and the name, sending `SelectStudy`, the chosen one an `actionButton` on `positiveBackground` and the others `MaterialsWindowView.verbButton`s (step 241's chosen-option look), or the line `This kit holds no study yet.`; then, when `kitStatus` is `Some`, its text in a wrapping `TextBlock` carrying `studyStatusLine`. (b) `studyUnknownsView (model) (dispatch) : IView`: a `ScrollViewer` scrolling both ways around a vertical `StackPanel` carrying `studyUnknownsPanel`, margin 8, holding in order: the study bar; while `model.kitWrites` (step 185) offers writes, the New study form: a `DockPanel` of `New study:` and a `TextBox` carrying `newStudyNameField` whose every change sends `SetNewStudyName`, a `WrapPanel` of one box per kit experiment carrying `newStudyExperimentToggle` and its name, sending `ToggleNewStudyExperiment`, a chosen one on `positiveBackground`, and `Create study` (`createStudyButton`, an `actionButton` on `positiveBackground`, present only when `StudyName.tryCreate` of the typed text answers `Ok name`, sending `StudyCommand (CreateStudy (name, <the chosen experiments>))`); then, for `model.selectedStudyOpt`: `Experiments: <its experiments' names, comma-separated>` (`studyExperimentsText`), and while writes are offered, one verb per kit experiment the study lacks, `Add <name>` (`addExperimentToStudyButton`, sending `StudyCommand (AddExperimentsToStudy (study.name, [ name ]))`), and one verb per material version that a sample of the study's items references (`model.tryItemModelChoice` answering `StackSampleChoice (sampleModel, _, sample)`, its `structure.referencedMaterialVersions`, step 61) and the study has not opened, `Open <its caption>` (`openMaterialButton`, sending `StudyCommand (OpenMaterial (study.name, version))`); then a `Grid` carrying `studyUnknownsGrid`, eight `Auto` columns `Owner`, `Parameter`, `State`, `Value`, `Bounds`, `σ`, `Scope` and `Link`, a semi-bold header row and one row per parameter of `model.studyContext.itemsUsedBy study` (step 366) in order as `ItemParameterRef`s, then per component of each opened material in study order as `MaterialParameterRef`s: the owner (the item's label, or `<the material's name> v<n>`); a box carrying `studyParameterRow` with the name, sending `EditStudyParameter` (step 411); the parameter's `gridCells` (step 241) for state, value, bounds and σ; for an unknown, a `ComboBox` carrying `studyParameterScopeChoice` over `ParameterScope.all`'s `text`s, `study.scopeOf` (step 362) selected, enabled by writes, whose change sends `StudyCommand (SetParameterScope (study.name, { parameter = <it>; scope = <the chosen> }))`, and `—` otherwise; for a link's follower, `= <its leader's studyParameterCaption>`, and for any other unknown a `ComboBox` carrying `studyParameterLinkChoice` over `(no link)` and every other unknown's caption, enabled by writes, whose choice of an unknown sends `StudyCommand (LinkParameters (study.name, { follower = <it>; leader = <the chosen> }))`. Fix and free are the editor's Known and Unknown, bounds and prior its fields: with `parameterEditOpt` open on a row the grid lists, `ItemsPanelView.parameterEditorView model draft setWith dispatch` (step 411) follows the grid, `setWith` being `fun state -> SetParameterState (id, name, state)` for an `ItemParameterRef (id, name)` and `fun state -> StudyCommand (SetOpenedMaterialParameter (study.name, version, { name = name; state = state }))` (step 409) for a `MaterialParameterRef (version, name)`. Without a chosen study the panel ends with `No study is chosen: create one above.`. No unlink verb is added: 001 §P names `LinkParameters` alone, and the follower keeps its own state. (5) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitWindowView.fs` (steps 242, 323): `UnknownsFlowStep` shows `StudyUnknownsView.studyUnknownsView model dispatch` keyed `unknowns`. No other surface changes. Tests. `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/TestAppScope.fs` (step 83) gains `studyKitIn (owner : FolderName) : TableAndElementRotationModel`, with a one-line doc citing spec 0050 S11.5, the one study fixture of the UI suite: over `freshAppContext owner` and a kit from `openedKitIn owner` (step 152), it records through the kit's library (`recordItem`, `recordSetup`, `recordExperiment`, steps 219, 260, 149) CPL1 and CPL2 over the built-in circular-polarizer model, each `c2.retardance` unknown from 1.5 within [1, 2], and a Phone over the intensity-detector model, `gain` unknown from 1000 within [100, 10000], one setup `Bench` holding them, and E1, E2 and E3, Science runs scanning the analyzer's R1 over 0…90° in 4 points (as step 310's facts record a one-axis scan), E1 and E3 attached at `data/e1.csv` and `data/e3.csv` (`Intensity series`, every row) and E2 without data; closes the kit, opens it again through `KitOpening.openKitAt`, loads it into an Inverse model over the context's stores as `InverseConstructorTests.inverse` builds its model (step 152), and sends `StudyCommand (CreateStudy (QZ-LR, [ E1; E2; E3 ]))`. New `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/StudyViewTests.fs`, `module StudyViewTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment, its screens mounted as `KitWindowTests` mounts `kitWindowView` (step 242). Without a trait: `the study view UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`: the eight fixed ids' texts and the derived ids of `QZ-LR`, `E1`, CPL1's `c2.retardance` and a test-local material version's `n1`; `the Unknowns step lists the study's item parameters and opened material components with their owner, state, bounds, sigma, scope and link`: over `studyKitIn` with a user absorbing crystal material saved through the context's material store and opened (`StudyCommand (OpenMaterial …)`) and CPL2's `c2.retardance` linked to CPL1's, on `UnknownsFlowStep`, the grid holds the rows of CPL1, CPL2 and the Phone in that order and then the material's fifteen components, the Phone's `gain` row reading `Unknown` and `Session`, CPL2's `c2.retardance` reading `= CPL1 c2.retardance`, and a known parameter's scope cell `—`. With trait `ui-smoke`: `typing a study name and pressing Create study records the study in the kit`: pressing `flowUnknownsStep`, typing `LR` into `newStudyNameField`, pressing E1's `newStudyExperimentToggle` and `createStudyButton` leaves the kit's folder holding `LR.study-json` over E1 and `studyChoice` of `LR` shown; `pressing a study parameter's row, Unknown and Set frees it in the kit`: pressing the Phone's `darkOffset` row, `parameterEditUnknownChoice`, typing `-1` and `1` into `parameterEditLowerField` and `parameterEditUpperField` and pressing `parameterEditSetButton` leaves `Phone.item-json` holding `darkOffset` unknown within [−1, 1] and its row reading `Unknown`. `KitWindowTests` (steps 242, 323): `the flow strip UiIds are the stable intent-named ids` also pins `FlowUnknownsStep`; `the flow strip shows Items, Setups and Experiments left of the surface its step shows` also finds, in the inverse window, the Unknowns box below Data and, on `UnknownsFlowStep`, `studyUnknownsPanel` present and `tableElementCanvas` absent, and in the Main window no Unknowns box; `a read-only window withholds every write control` finds in `studyUnknownsView` over the read-only model no `createStudyButton`, no `addExperimentToStudyButton` and every `studyParameterScopeChoice` disabled. `KitWindowModelTests` (steps 238, 323): `the flow strip's steps follow 001's order and a window opens on Setups` lists Items, Setups, Experiments, Data and Unknowns with their captions; `the Data step is the Inverse constructor's alone, and leaving the Inverse constructor leaves it` also finds `stepsOf ForwardConstructor` without Unknowns, `ShowFlowStep UnknownsFlowStep` over `initMain ()` changing nothing, and `SwitchConstructorMode ForwardConstructor` from `UnknownsFlowStep` answering `ExperimentsFlowStep`. `ScrollExtentTests` gains `the kit window's Unknowns step leaves everything reachable`: `assertReachable "KitWindowUnknowns"` (`ScrollExtentTests.fs:89`) over a `HostWindow` running `kitWindowView` over `studyKitIn`'s model on `UnknownsFlowStep`, its material opened, the editor open on CPL1's `c2.retardance`. All choice construction and matching in this step MUST use step 216's payloads, including the resolved ItemModelVersion for source, ideal-polarizer and stack choices. Fixtures MUST obtain those versions from step 210's shipped model entries; runtime resolution MUST use the stored version through ItemModelProxy, never manufacture a model or use a preset/sample as the model. Existing parameter values and optical results MUST be preserved.

**Acceptance.** After the Unknowns step lands, the Inverse constructor's flow strip MUST show Unknowns after Data and the Main constructor's none, and `studyUnknownsView` MUST show the kit's studies, the New study form, the chosen study's experiments, material offers and unknowns table (owner, state, value, bounds, σ, scope, link) under their `ConstructorUiId`s, sending the study messages and opening the shared parameter editor, every write control withheld under a read-only kit; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including the changed `the flow strip's steps follow 001's order and a window opens on Setups` and `the Data step is the Inverse constructor's alone, and leaving the Inverse constructor leaves it`; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `typing a study name and pressing Create study records the study in the kit` and `pressing a study parameter's row, Unknown and Set frees it in the kit`, the count rising by 2; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the study view UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`, `the Unknowns step lists the study's item parameters and opened material components with their owner, state, bounds, sigma, scope and link` and `the kit window's Unknowns step leaves everything reachable`, the count rising by 3, and the changed `the flow strip UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`, `the flow strip shows Items, Setups and Experiments left of the surface its step shows` and `a read-only window withholds every write control`; and build, elevation and the twenty s40 invariants MUST pass.
